From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 05:56:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the CPU topology and caches

Without cache nodes the kernel assumes that every cache above L1 is shared
by all CPUs, but each A733 core has its own L2.

Describe the six Cortex-A55 and two Cortex-A76 cores as one DynamIQ cluster
with a shared 1 MiB L3, with the cache geometry the cores report in
CCSIDR_EL1. One cluster, not one per core type: all eight cores report the
same cluster affinity in MPIDR_EL1 and share the DSU and its L3, and no
cache below the L3 is shared by a subset of them. The two core types
differ in capacity and clock, not in topology.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; cacheinfo reports 32 KiB
L1 and 128 KiB L2 per A55, 64 KiB L1 and 256 KiB L2 per A76, each L2
private, and a 1 MiB L3 shared by all eight CPUs.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 181 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 181 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 908219081e5d..7d6fd3962e8e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -16,12 +16,55 @@ cpus {
 		#address-cells = <1>;
 		#size-cells = <0>;
 
+		cpu-map {
+			cluster0 {
+				core0 {
+					cpu = <&cpu0>;
+				};
+
+				core1 {
+					cpu = <&cpu1>;
+				};
+
+				core2 {
+					cpu = <&cpu2>;
+				};
+
+				core3 {
+					cpu = <&cpu3>;
+				};
+
+				core4 {
+					cpu = <&cpu4>;
+				};
+
+				core5 {
+					cpu = <&cpu5>;
+				};
+
+				core6 {
+					cpu = <&cpu6>;
+				};
+
+				core7 {
+					cpu = <&cpu7>;
+				};
+			};
+		};
+
 		cpu0: cpu@0 {
 			compatible = "arm,cortex-a55";
 			device_type = "cpu";
 			reg = <0x000>;
 			enable-method = "psci";
 			capacity-dmips-mhz = <530>;
+			i-cache-size = <32768>;
+			i-cache-line-size = <64>;
+			i-cache-sets = <128>;
+			d-cache-size = <32768>;
+			d-cache-line-size = <64>;
+			d-cache-sets = <128>;
+			next-level-cache = <&l2_cache0>;
 		};
 
 		cpu1: cpu@100 {
@@ -30,6 +73,13 @@ cpu1: cpu@100 {
 			reg = <0x100>;
